# Ocean cost on RaceArena_Pro. Run:  bench.cmd bench\plans\ocean.bench
#
# Question: why is FPS low when only a sliver of water is in the PVS?
#
# RaceArena_Pro is the worst case and the reason this plan exists. Its BSP has
# 27 distinct water planes; the 8 largest get promoted (OCEAN_MAX_SURFACES), and
# the biggest is the z=7946 "donut" spanning x -27567..25746 / y -32040..29196.
# The player spawns at z=7819, INSIDE that donut's hollow, so almost no water is
# on screen - exactly the case being investigated.
#
# Read these columns first:
#   sea_draws  clipmap draws encoded (one per promoted surface the frustum kept)
#   sea_tris   triangles those draws submitted
# The clipmap is camera-centred, not footprint-sized, so one visible sliver
# submits that whole surface's mesh and the shape mask then discards the
# fragments outside the real outline. If sea_tris is in the hundreds of
# thousands while barely any water is visible, that is the finding.
#
# And these GPU passes:
#   ocean_sim      FFT cascades + wind-foam transport. Runs whether or not any
#                  water is visible (new pass; it used to be unattributed).
#   ocean_surface  the clipmap draw itself.
#   ocean_optics   scene capture + underwater composite.

map       RaceArena_Pro
launches  3        # single runs vary +/-15%
settle    3
sample    5
timeout   420      # big map, cold caches

cfg r_gpuTimings 1
cfg r_perfTrace 1
# Force the general renderer in every case. Without this, `ocean_off` would also
# become FastBaseline-eligible (plan.rs requires !ocean_enabled), and the
# baseline would measure two changes at once instead of one.
cfg r_worldPath unified

# Spawn (info_player_start), two facings. Both stand on solid ground inside the
# hollow; only the amount of water on screen differs.
spot hollow_e  -1985 -1238 7819 0
spot hollow_w  -1985 -1238 7819 180

# --- cases ------------------------------------------------------------------
# r_ocean goes in the cfg: turning it on live needs the world's ocean pipeline
# variant already compiled, so the map has to load in the state being measured.
case ocean_off      cfg:r_ocean=0
case ocean_on       cfg:r_ocean=1

# Geometry lever. Low mesh = 1 m inner cells instead of 0.25 m, roughly a
# quarter of the triangles for identical screen coverage. A large win here means
# vertex/primitive bound; no change means the cost is in the fragments that the
# shape mask discards.
case mesh_low       cfg:r_ocean=1 r_oceanMeshQuality=0

# Simulation levers. NOTE: r_oceanUpdates 0 does NOT disable the sim - ocean.rs
# treats 0 as "always due", so it runs the FFT every frame. 1 is the cheap end.
case sim_1hz        cfg:r_ocean=1 r_oceanUpdates=1
case sim_60hz       cfg:r_ocean=1 r_oceanUpdates=60
case fft_256        cfg:r_ocean=1 r_oceanMapSize=256

# Per-frame compute that is not gated by visibility at all.
case windfoam_off   cfg:r_ocean=1 r_oceanWindFoam=0
case spray_off      cfg:r_ocean=1 r_oceanSeaSpray=0

# Underwater optics: the scene capture runs whenever the map has any ocean
# surface, and the composite only when the camera is submerged.
case optics_cheap   cfg:r_ocean=1 r_oceanRefraction=0 r_oceanCaustics=0 r_oceanDepthDarkening=0

# Everything cheap at once. If this still sits far below ocean_off, the cost is
# structural (clipmap size, mask discard, the passes render_ocean forces on) and
# not in any one setting.
case all_cheap      cfg:r_ocean=1 r_oceanMeshQuality=0 r_oceanUpdates=1 r_oceanMapSize=256 r_oceanWindFoam=0 r_oceanSeaSpray=0 r_oceanRefraction=0 r_oceanCaustics=0 r_oceanDepthDarkening=0
